#: ../../source/fs.scandir_README.md:147
msgid "`old` and `modern` mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fs.scandir_README.md:149
msgid ""
"This package has two modes that are used depending on the environment and"
" parameters of use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fs.scandir_README.md:151
msgid "old"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fs.scandir_README.md:153
msgid "Node.js below `10.10` or when the `stats` option is enabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fs.scandir_README.md:155
msgid ""
"When working in the old mode, the directory is read first (`fs.readdir`),"
" then the type of entries is determined (`fs.lstat` and/or `fs.stat` for "
"symbolic links)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fs.scandir_README.md:157
msgid "modern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fs.scandir_README.md:159
msgid "Node.js 10.10+ and the `stats` option is disabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fs.scandir_README.md:161
msgid ""
"In the modern mode, reading the directory (`fs.readdir` with the "
"`withFileTypes` option) is combined with obtaining information about its "
"entries. An additional call for symbolic links (`fs.stat`) is still "
"present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fs.scandir_README.md:163
msgid "This mode makes fewer calls to the file system. It's faster."
msgstr ""

